        "by": "human",
        "reason": "attempt_0004/concept.sql:31 and :41 map Observation.effective_datetime and effective_period_start through CAST(TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REGEXP_REPLACE(...), pinned-format) AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). The offset-aware parser re-renders the instant in spark.sql.session.timeZone and the pinned format silently NULLs any shape it misses (date-only values especially), so the recorded exact match holds only at session zone America/New_York and is not reproducible elsewhere. This is the same defect the first reopen was meant to clear; attempt_0004 still carries it. Replace both with a bare TRY_CAST(col AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ), nothing wrapped around it. The REGEXP_REPLACE at :58-59 is unrelated trailing-zero stripping on quantity_value and must stay. mimic_utils validate-demo now refuses this construction (sql_lint datetime-parser).",
